  "Question": "A city charges 2 yuan per tonne for monthly water usage up to 10 tonnes, and 3 yuan per tonne for the portion exceeding 10 tonnes. A household uses $x$ tonnes of water ($x>10$) and must pay $y$ yuan. Which expression gives $y$ as a function of $x$? ( )",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$y=3x$",
    "B": "$y=3x+20$",
    "C": "$y=2x+10$",
    "D": "$y=3x-10$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The first 10 tonnes cost 20 yuan, and the excess $(x-10)$ tonnes cost 3 yuan per tonne: $y=20+3(x-10)=3x-10$.",
